, handoff) [...] # pi-agent-extensions [...] A collection of extensions for the pi coding agent. [...] | Extension | Type | Description | Status | [...] | --- | --- | --- | --- | | **sessions [...] | Command | Quick session picker with `/sessions` | ✅ Stable | | **ask_user [...] Tool | LLM can ask [...] ⚙️ Beta | | **handoff** | Command | Goal-driven context transfer `/handoff` | ✅\nSource: jayshah5696/pi-agent-extensions (https://github.com/jayshah5696/pi-agent-extensions/)\n\nPi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt Pi to your workflows, not the other way around. Customize Pi with extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes. Bundle them as Pi packages and share via npm or git. [...] Pi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub-agents and plan mode. Ask Pi to build what you want, or install a package that does it your way. [...] Prompt templates: Reusable prompts as Markdown files. Type`/name` to expand. See prompt templates. [...] Features t\nSource: Pi Coding Agent (https://pi.dev/)\n\n**Pi package with custom extensions, themes, and configurations for the Pi Coding Agent** [...] ### Pi Package (recommended) [...] ```bash pi install git:github.com/VTSTech/pi-coding-agent ``` [...] Pi clones the repo, auto-discovers the `extensions/` and `themes/` directories, and [...] automatically. Restart Pi and you're done. [...] ```bash pi install git:github.com/VTSTech/pi-coding-agent [...] ### Individual npm packages [...] Each extension is published separately to npm. Install only what\nSource: VTSTech/pi-coding-agent (https://github.com/VTSTech/pi-coding-agent)\n\n<p align=\"center\"> <a href=\"https://discord.com/invite/3cU7Bz4UPx\"><img alt=\"Discord\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/badge/discord-community-5865F2?style=flat-square&logo=discord&logoColor=white\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent\"><img alt=\"npm\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/npm/v/@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent?style=flat-square\" /></a>