g/pi-depo)\n\nDeclarative package manager for Pi Coding Agent - skills, extensions, hooks, MCP servers [...] # pi-depo (pd) [...] Declarative package manager for Pi Coding Agent. Manage skills, extensions, and MCP servers from a single`kit.yml`, synced across machines via GitHub Gist. [...] ``` pd login pd init # → \"Bootstrap from someone's public gist?\" → y # → \"GitHub username or username/profile:\" → fulgidus # → imports their kit.yml, offers to sync immediately ``` [...] pd login [...] authenticate pd init\nSource: pi-depo 0.1.44 on npm - Libraries.io - security & maintenance data for open source software (https://libraries.io/npm/pi-depo)\n\n: - [...] +```bash +pd # sync everything (default command) +pd sync # same -| Command | Description | -|---------|-------------| -| `pkit init` | Bootstrap `kit.yml` from current Pi installation | -| `pkit sync` | Desired state → real state. Idempotent. | -| `pkit status` | Show package status (synced/missing/disabled/orphan) | -| `pkit diff` | Dry-run sync - show what would change | -| `pkit verify` | Run verify checks for all packages | -| `pkit upgrade` | Update non-pinned packages to latest \nSource: feat: pd init imports from public gist + full README rewrite · fb0e506 · fulgidus/pi-depo (https://github.com/fulgidus/pi-depo/commit/fb0e506d9ee148219367b7282648c7115582583e)\n\nPi Coding Agent [...] Pi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt Pi to your workflows, not the other way around. Customize Pi with extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes. Bundle them as Pi packages and share via npm or git. [...] Pi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub-agents and plan mode. Ask Pi to build what you want, or install a package that does it your way. [...] Pi isn't a sealed product. If you need a command, tool, provider, workflow, or UI tweak, just\nSource: Pi Coding Agent (https://pi.dev/)\n\nPi Coding Agent [...] Pi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt Pi to your workflows, not the other way around. Customize Pi with extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes. Bundle them as Pi packages and share via npm or git. [...] Pi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub-agents and plan mode. Ask Pi to build what you want, or install a package that does it your way. [...] Pi isn't a sealed product. If you need a command, tool, provider, workflow, or UI tweak, just\nSource: Pi Coding Agent (https://shittycodingagent.ai/)\n\nCoding agent CLI with read, bash, edit, write tools and session management forked from @mariozechner/pi-coding-agent [...] > _Current focus: at [...] moment i'm deep in refactoring internals, and need to focus._ --- pi.dev domain graciously donated by exe.dev Pi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt pi to your workflows, not the other way around, without having to fork and modify pi internals. Extend it with TypeScript Extensions, Skills, Prompt Templates, and Themes. Put your extensions, \nSource: @vandeepunk/pi-coding-agent (https://registry.npmjs.org/@vandeepunk/pi-coding-agent)\n\nI have been running OpenCode and Hermes Agent for a while now, but Pi kept coming up in conversations. People on Reddit and Hacker News kept calling it \"the minimal one that does not get in your way.\" After two weeks of daily use, I see why. Pi is a terminal coding agent built by Mario Zechner that stays small at the core. You install it, point it at a project, and start working. Everything else — memory, MCP support, sub-agents, themes, skills — gets added through extensions you actually choose\nSource: Pi Coding Agent Setup Guide: Install, Configure Models, and Best Extensions (https://www.bitdoze.com/pi-coding-agent-setup-guide/)\n\n# Repository: capdevc/pi-codex-profile (fork of Graffioh/pi-codex-profile) [...] # pi-codex-profile [...] Codex performance profile for pi coding agent. No command needed: once the extension is loaded (`/reload`), it works automatically when your active model is Codex. [...] ### 1) Codex operating profile (auto-injected) [...] When a Codex model is active, the extension appends a comprehensive Codex profile to the system prompt. It includes high-impact coding guidance adapted from the Codex Prom\nSource: capdevc/pi-codex-profile (https://github.com/capdevc/pi-codex-profile)\n\n# Repository: zhouzhuojie/pi-agents (fork of michalvavra/agents) [...] Configuration for pi AI coding agents. [...] # Agent Configuration [...] Configuration for AI coding agents. [...] ## [pi][pi-coding-agent] extensions [...] - `skill-dollar.ts`: suggests `$skill-name` completions in the editor and injects skill usage guidance when mentioned. Idea from Codex. [...] ```bash ln -sf {baseDir}/AGENTS.md ~/.pi/agent/AGENTS.md ln -sf {baseDir}/skills ~/.pi/agent/skills ln -sf {baseDir}/agents/pi/pro\nSource: zhouzhuojie/pi-agents (https://github.com/zhouzhuojie/pi-agents)\n\n* pi-coding-agent: Coding Agent CLI [...] # pi-coding-agent: Coding Agent CLI [...] The `@mariozechner/pi-coding-agent` package provides an interactive terminal-based coding assistant with tool execution, session persistence, and extensibility. This page documents the overall architecture, core abstractions, and how the system components interact. It serves as the architectural overview for the coding-agent package. [...] The coding agent is built around `AgentSession`, which orchestrates the ag\nSource: pi-coding-agent: Coding Agent CLI | badlogic/pi-mono | DeepWiki (https://deepwiki.com/badlogic/pi-mono/4-pi-coding-agent:-coding-agent-cli)","results":[{"title":"pi-depo","url":"https://registry.npmjs.org/pi-depo","snippet":""},{"title":"pi-depo 0.1.44 on npm - Libraries.io - security & maintenance data for open source software","url":"https://libraries.io/npm/pi-depo","snippet":""},{"title":"feat: pd init imports from public gist + full README rewrite · fb0e506 · fulgidus/pi-depo","url":"https://github.com/fulgidus/pi-depo/commit/fb0e506d9ee148219367b7282648c7115582583e","snippet":""},{"title":"Pi Coding Agent","url":"ht