{"type":"message","id":"f6555f5d","parentId":"703fdafa","timestamp":"2026-05-16T13:03:19.174Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_kVkHhbEkFj9O5en22H020qQB|fc_02f887b473d5faa9016a086b1133e08190bd60b953fd340032","name":"log_experiment","arguments":{"commit":"24d4c15","metric":200,"status":"keep","description":"Validate domain-flow strategy: authored skills over niche Pi packages","metrics":{"sources_reviewed":200},"asi":{"hypothesis":"For marketing, video, UI/UX consulting, and infra/IPsec/pentesting, the Pi ecosystem likely has few mature domain-specific extension packages; Atlas should compose generic tools with Atlas-authored skills/prompts rather than hunt for niche packages.","new_findings":"Searches for SEO/marketing, video creation/editing, UI/UX design, and pentest/IPsec/infrastructure surfaced mostly generic workflow packages, web access, subagents, pi-agent-flow, safety guards, and noisy/irrelevant catalog hits. Heart of Gold Toolkit is the main broad skill bundle with relevant Guide content engine skills (blog/LinkedIn/content pipeline) and Babel Fish media skills (audio/image/visualize/linkedin carousel), but installing the whole package adds 32 skills and Pi-native commands; better to selectively install or borrow patterns after review.","recommendation_shift":"Flow manifests should separate tools from domain playbooks. Tools: browser, web access, markdown preview, subagents, maybe media generation. Domain expertise should live in Atlas-owned skills/templates: SEO audit, content calendar, SSG launch checklist, video script/storyboard/edit checklist, UI/UX heuristic audit, IPsec/pentest rules-of-engagement and report template.","overfit_guard":"Did not force package adoption where search evidence was weak; rejected popularity-by-association and kept domain logic in auditable Atlas text."}}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":546,"output":333,"cacheRead":130560,"ca