{"type":"message","id":"9337fb6b","parentId":"731795b8","timestamp":"2026-05-16T13:03:28.342Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next iteration complete.\n\n- Hypothesis: domain flows should be mostly **Atlas-authored skills/templates + generic tools**, not niche Pi packages.\n- Researched package availability for:\n  - marketing/SEO/content\n  - video creation/editing\n  - UI/UX consulting\n  - infra/IPsec/pentesting\n  - Heart of Gold Toolkit as broad skill bundle\n- `run_experiment`: `research_coverage=200`\n- `log_experiment`: kept\n- Commit: `ac3a3ba`\n- Confidence: `4.0× noise floor`\n\nKey finding:\n- Pi ecosystem has few mature, directly domain-specific packages for those flows.\n- Better Atlas architecture:\n  - Generic tools installed on demand: browser, web access, markdown preview, subagents, maybe media generation.\n  - Domain expertise lives in Atlas-owned skills/templates.\n\nPotential Atlas-authored skills:\n- `seo-audit`\n- `content-calendar`\n- `ssg-launch-checklist`\n- `video-script-storyboard`\n- `video-edit-review`\n- `uiux-heuristic-audit`\n- `ipsec-consulting-checklist`\n- `pentest-roe-report`\n\nHeart of Gold has relevant content/media skills, but whole-package install adds 32 skills + commands. Better to review/selectively borrow patterns, not install globally.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02f887b473d5faa9016a086b1b45008190b7c6a6159ddeb790\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":736,"output":274,"cacheRead":131072,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":132082,"cost":{"input":0.00368,"output":0.00822,"cacheRead":0.065536,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.077436}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1778936602287,"responseId":"resp_02f887b473d5faa9016a086b1a6fcc81908306bb774fef7de6"}}
