pe | Default | Description | |---------|------|---------|-------------| | `shellPath` | string | - | Custom shell path (e.g., for Cygwin on Windows) | | `shellCommandPrefix` | string | \nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md)\n\n### Package Commands [...] ```bash pi install <source> [-l] # Install package, -l for project-local pi remove <source> [-l] # Remove package pi uninstall <source> [-l] # Alias for remove pi update [source|self|pi] # Update pi and packages; skips pinned packages pi update --extensions # Update packages only pi update --self # Update pi only pi update --extension <src> # Update one package pi list # List installed packages pi config # Enable/disable package resources ``` [...] | Variable | Descrip\nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md)\n\n| Location | Scope | |----------|-------| [...] | `~/. [...] /agent/settings [...] ### Pi Packages [...] ```bash pi install npm:@foo/pi-tools pi install npm:@foo/pi-tools@1.2.3 # pinned version [...] pi update # [...] pi update --extensions [...] pi config # enable/ [...] extensions, skills, prompts, themes [...] Packages install to `~/.pi/agent/git/` (git) or global npm. Use `-l` for project-local installs (`.pi/git/`, `.pi/npm/`). Git packages install dependencies with `npm install --omit=dev`\nSource: heads/main/packages/coding-agent/README.md at refs · badlogic/pi-mono (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/refs/heads/main/packages/coding-agent/README.md)\n\nPi is distributed as an npm package: [...] ```bash npm install -g @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent ``` [...] Then start pi in the project directory you want it to work on: [...] ```bash cd /path/to/project pi ``` [...] ## Give pi project instructions [...] Pi loads context files at startup. Add an `AGENTS.md` file to tell it how to work in a project: [...] ```markdown # Project Instructions - Run `npm run check` after code changes. - Do not run production migrations locally. - Keep responses conc\nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/quickstart.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/quickstart.md)\n\nPi is a minimal terminal coding harness. Adapt Pi to your workflows, not the other way around. Customize Pi with extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes. Bundle them as Pi packages and share via npm or git. [...] Pi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub-agents and plan mode. Ask Pi to build what you want, or install a package that does it your way. [...] AGENTS.md: Project instructions loaded at startup from`~/.pi/agent/`, parent directories, and the current directory\nSource: Pi Coding Agent (https://pi.dev/)\n\nPi is a [...] terminal coding harness. It is designed to [...] the core while being extended through TypeScript extensions, skills, prompt templates, themes [...] On linux or mac you can install Pi with curl: [...] ```bash curl -fsSL https://pi.dev/install.sh | sh ``` [...] Or alternatively with npm: [...] ```bash npm install -g @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent ``` [...] Then run it in a project directory: [...] ```bash pi ``` [...] Authenticate with `/login` for subscription providers, or set an\nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/index.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/index.md)\n\nPi uses JSON settings files with project settings overriding global settings. [...] | Location | Scope | |----------|-------| | `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` | Global (all projects) | | `.pi/settings.json` | Project (current directory) | [...] Edit directly or use `/settings` for common options. [...] | Setting | Type | Default | Description | |---------|------|---------|-------------| | `shellPath` | string | - | Custom shell path (e.g., for Cygwin on Windows) | | `shellCommandPrefix` | string | \nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md)\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n1. packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md\n\n2. packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md\n\n3. packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md\n\n4. heads/main/packages/coding-agent/README.md at refs · badlogic/pi-mono\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/refs/heads/main/packages/coding-agent/README.md\n\n5. packages/coding-agent/docs/quickstart.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/quickstart.md\n\n6. Pi Coding Agent\n   https://pi.dev/\n\n7. packages/coding-agent/docs/index.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/index.md\n\n8. packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md\n\n## Query: \"\"pi config\" enable disable resources Pi Coding Agent packages filtering\"\n\nPi packages bundle extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes so you can share them through npm or git. A package can declare resources in `package.json` under the `pi` key, or use conventional directories. [...] - Install and Manage - Package Sources - Creating a Pi Package - Package Structure - Dependencies - Package Filtering - Enable and Disable Resources - Scope and Deduplication [...] ## Package Filtering [...] Filter what a package loads using the object form in settings: ```json { \nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md)\n\n```bash pi install <source> [-l] # Install package, -l for project-local pi remove <source> [-l] # Remove package pi uninstall <source> [-l] # Alias for remove pi update [source|self|pi] # Update pi and packages; skips pinned packages pi update --extensions # Update packages only pi update --self # Update pi only pi update --extension <src> # Update one package pi list # List installed packages pi config # Enable/disable package resources ``` [...] See Pi Packages for package sources and securit\nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md)\n\n----------|-------| [...] These settings define where to load extensions, skills, prompts, and themes from. Paths in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` resolve relative to `~/.pi/agent`. Paths in `.pi/settings.json` resolve relative to `.pi`. Absolute paths and `~` are supported. [...] | Setting | Type | Default | Description | |---------|------|---------|-------------| | `packages` | array | `[]` | npm/git packages to load resources from | | `extensions` | string[] | `[]` | Local extension file paths \nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md)\n\n----------|-------| [...] These settings define where to load extensions, skills, prompts, and themes from. Paths in `~/.pi/agent/settings.json` resolve relative to `~/.pi/agent`. Paths in `.pi/settings.json` resolve relative to `.pi`. Absolute paths and `~` are supported. [...] | Setting | Type | Default | Description | |---------|------|---------|-------------| | `packages` | array | `[]` | npm/git packages to load resources from | | `extensions` | string[] | `[]` | Local extension file paths \nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md)\n\n## Empty array in package filter should disable all resources, not fall back to defaults [...] So I added github.com/tmustier/pi-extensions/ to my local setup, and specifically configured that i only want the arcade extension, so my `settings.json` looks like this: [...] ``` \"packages\": [ \"/Users/lars/GitHub/agent-stuff\", { \"source\": \"git:github.com/tmustier/pi-extensions\", \"extensions\": [ \"arcade/spice-invaders.ts\", \"arcade/picman.ts\", \"arcade/ping.ts\", \"arcade/tetris.ts\", \"arcade/mario-not/mar\nSource: Empty array in package filter should disable all resources, not fall back to defaults · Issue #1044 · badlogic/pi-mono (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1044)\n\n- `pi install npm:pi-package-test` - `pi config` - navigate to `status-bar` and enable. - Hit `Esc` key - `pi config` (again) - navigate to `status-bar` [...] Path B: use the manifest disable statements to hide them in `pi config` so the user is never presented an option to enable. [...] It is confusing for the user to see an option on `pi config`, enable it and not see it being applied, even more confusing going back to the config screen and seeing it disabled. [...] as mentioned there are two \nSource: Overriding manifest disable for dependency extensions · Issue #951 · badlogic/pi-mono (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/951)\n\n## Add pi config TUI to manage package resources [...] Add a new `pi config` CLI command that opens a TUI for enabling and disabling package resources and top-level resources. It should list all resources with enabled state based on settings patterns and update user or project settings using `!` and `+` patterns. [...] - **CLI**: Add `pi config` command to `main.ts` and update help output. Mirror the `--resume` pattern by using a standalone TUI in `packages/coding-agent/src/cli/config-selector.t\nSource: Add pi config TUI to manage package resources · Issue #938 (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/938)\n\n## Resource Discovery [...] When a package is installed, Pi looks for resources in the following locations within the package root: [...] `skills/` [...] `prompts/` [...] You can manually configure packages in `settings.json`: ```json { \"packages\": [ \"npm:pi-skills\", { \"source\": \"git:github.com/org/repo\", \"skills\": [\"relevant-skill\"], \"extensions\": [] } ] } ``` [...] The object form allows filtering which resources are loaded (allowlisting). If a field is omitted, all resources of that type are \nSource: docs/packages.md at main · Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust (https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust/blob/main/docs/packages.md)\n\n---\n\n**Sources:**\n1. packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/packages.md\n\n2. packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/usage.md\n\n3. packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md\n\n4. packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi\n   https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md\n\n5. Empty array in package filter should disable all resources, not fall back to defaults · Issue #1044 · badlogic/pi-mono\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/1044\n\n6. Overriding manifest disable for dependency extensions · Issue #951 · badlogic/pi-mono\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/951\n\n7. Add pi config TUI to manage package resources · Issue #938\n   https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/issues/938\n\n8. docs/packages.md at main · Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust\n   https://