hat provide extensions, skills, prompt templates, and themes. [...] Pi supports three types of package sources: [...] 1. **npm**: `npm:package-name` or `npm:@org/package` (optionally `@version`) 2. **git**: `git:host/owner/repo` or just `https://github.com/owner/repo` (optionally `@ref`) 3. **local**: path to a directory (e.g. `../my-package`) [...] Install a package globally (user scope): [...] ```bash pi install npm:pi-skills pi install git:github.com/someuser/\nSource: docs/packages.md at main · Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust (https://github.com/Dicklesworthstone/pi_agent_rust/blob/main/docs/packages.md)\n\nPi ships with powerful defaults but skips features like sub agents and plan mode. Instead, you can ask pi to build what you want [...] package that matches your workflow. [...] ### Pi Packages [...] Bundle and share extensions, skills, prompts, and themes via npm or git. Find packages on npmjs.com or Discord. [...] Security: Pi packages run with full system access. Extensions execute arbitrary code, and skills can instruct the model to perform any action including running executables. Review sou\nSource: pi-mono/packages/coding-agent at main · badlogic/pi-mono · GitHub (https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono/tree/main/packages/coding-agent)\n\nall projects) | [...] directory) | [...] | Setting | Type | Default | Description | |---------|------|---------|-------------| | `theme` | string | `\"dark\"` | Theme name (`\"dark\"`, `\"light\"`, or custom) | | `quietStartup` | boolean | `false` | Hide startup header | | `collapseChangelog` | boolean | `false` | Show condensed changelog after updates | | `enableInstallTelemetry` | boolean | `true` | Send an anonymous install/update version ping after first install or changelog-detected updates. This\nSource: packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md at main · earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/docs/settings.md)\n\n/update telemetry [...] changelog- [...] update, sends an 