GitHub for cleanup purposes. After that, I’ll need to run the experiment and log the results. I have to be careful since logging will commit changes as well, which makes it a bit tricky. So, I’ll definitely use the GitHub command to create the issue. It feels like a necessary mutation to keep things aligned and organized.\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_bjQh8u62TqppFO481FY2ZBFV|fc_02f887b473d5faa9016a086bc6deb481908f7e82410244deff","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cat > /tmp/atlas-baseline-issue.md <<'EOF'\n## Problem\n\n`atlas-config` is intended to keep Pi minimal and cherry-picked, but current `pi/.pi/agent/settings.json` has a LazyPi-sized global package surface. That increases startup/context/tool clutter and makes it harder to reason about which capabilities are always active.\n\n## Proposed direction\n\nSplit Pi configuration into:\n\n1. **Minimal global baseline** — packages/extensions that should be active in almost every Pi session.\n2. **Optional core** — packages enabled only if explicitly desired globally.\n3. **Flow manifests** — packages/skills/prompts installed project-locally or on-demand via `/atlas-flow`.\n\n## Proposed global baseline\n\nKeep global:\n\n- local custom extensions:\n  - `recall-compaction.ts`\n  - `recall-extract.ts`\n  - `superset-hooks.ts`\n  - future `atlas-flow.ts`\n- `npm:pi-ask-user`\n- `npm:pi-subagents`\n- `npm:pi-prompt-template-model`\n\nConsider optional-global only if used every session:\n\n- `npm:pi-mcp-adapter`\n- `npm:pi-web-access`\n- `npm:pi-claude-cli`\n\nMove to flow/profile manifests:\n\n- UI/review: `plannotator`, `slopchop`, `interactive-shell`, browser tools, markdown preview\n- Research: `autoresearch`, `ralph-wiggum`\n- Writing/marketing: `markdown-preview`, `web-access`, reviewed Heart-of-Gold Guide subset\n- Personal UX: `powerbar`, `usage`, `btw`, `raw-paste`, `todo`\n- Themes: separate non-functional profile, not core\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Document current global package classification.\n- [ ] Create `pi/.pi/agent/flows/` manifests for optional profiles before removing global packages.\n- [ ] Keep package sources pinned where possible.\n- [ ] Preserve a rollback path for the current settings.\n- [ ] Update `README.md` or a plan doc with how to restore optional profiles.\n- [ ] Run `just status` after changes to verify stow behavior.\n\n## Safety notes\n\nDo not remove packages until matching flow manifests exist. Prefer project-local installs from `/atlas-flow` unless a package has a clear every-session justification.\nEOF\ngh issue create --repo edheltzel/atlas-config --title \"Split Pi settings into minimal global baseline and on-demand flow profiles\" --body-file /tmp/atlas-baseline-issue.md","timeout":60}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input":3527,"output":627,"cacheRead":168960,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":173114,"cost":{"input":0.017635,"output":0.01881,"cacheRead":0.08448,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.120925}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778936770715,"responseId":"resp_02f887b473d5faa9016a086bc2e4248190af4605520daaeff2"}}
